  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0001] Round money only with round_money: Always round monetary results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 1x, 1 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0002] Normalize unit prices with to_money and ZERO: In ledgerly/invoice.py, wrap line unit prices with to_money() and accumulate sums starting from ledgerly.money.ZERO, as line_total and invoice_total do, so Decimal arithmetic stays consistent.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 1x, 1 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0003] Raise BillingError with stable error codes: Reject invalid billing input by raising `BillingError` from `ledgerly.errors` with a short snake_case code such as `invalid_state`, `invalid_quantity` or `negative_amount`, plus a repr of the offending value.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0004] Guard mutations on invoice draft status: Before mutating an invoice, check `invoice.status != \"draft\"` and raise `BillingError(\"invalid_state\", ...)` including the invoice id and status, matching `issue_invoice` in `ledgerly/invoice.py`.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
